{
  "name": "scatter_balochi",
  "description": "Balochi — an Iranian language of south-western Pakistan, south-eastern Iran, and southern Afghanistan, written in Perso-Arabic-derived script. Like Pashto, Balochi has acquired the subcontinental retroflex set via the north-western contact zone — retroflex stops (ʈ, ɖ) and the retroflex flap (ɽ), though without the full retroflex fricative / nasal / lateral complement Pashto carries. Voiceless stops at 4 places (bilabial, dental, retroflex, velar). Voiced at 4. Two nasals. Voiceless fricatives f, s, ʃ, h; voiced z, ʒ. Two affricates tʃ, dʒ. Lateral /l/, trill /r/, retroflex flap /ɽ/. Inventory drawn from Jahani & Korn (2009).",
